/* The UNSAT arm carries no certificate of its own: `unsat_terminal` and the
   level-zero stable facts it would need are gone, and `cnf_unsat(n, F)` is a
   visible conjunct of the contract's UNSAT disjunct where the reader sees it.
   What remains is the frame, the bounds, and the coherence facts inside
   store_cnf -- so this rule is rule 43/44 with the assignment component
   unconstrained instead of pinned to J.

   `ranks` stays a head pattern variable although nothing in the action uses
   it: the four arm cores keep the complete fourteen-ghost vector so they stay
   uniform in shape.  Unused entry ghosts are already the norm here -- 43/44
   never mention `snap` or `live` either. */

