/* --- Helper-contract vocabulary (Tasks 8A-8D) -----------------------------
   Rules 49-56 shred the four helper-contract wrappers.  One unconditional
   fixed-head core(1) pair per C-visible predicate, both sides, per the file's
   stated discipline: the bundles are notation, not a reasoning step.

   Emitter-after-consumer id discipline holds: 49/50 emit sat_header_rep /
   var_header_rep / clause_header_rep (consumed by 15-22),
   unconstrained_Assignment (39/40) and solver_arrays_rep (13/14); 51/52 emit
   IntArray::full and installed_rows_capacity_rep (3-6); 53/54 emit
   variable_arrays_rep (11/12) and pending_backjump_rep (a leaf);
   55/56 emit solver_state, consumed by 49/50.  Every emitted head has a
   strictly lower consuming id.

   `?original_count` in 53/54 is a head-only pattern variable, unused in the
   action -- precedented by `?snap`/`?ranks` in 43/44. */

